   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What you are good at",
     "texto": [
      "**Se me da bien** (one thing) and **se me dan bien** (several things) talk about your skills. The verb agrees with the skill, not with you:\n\n- **El inglés** se me da bien.\n- **Las matemáticas** se me dan bien.\n- **Cantar** se me da mal. With an infinitive, the verb is always singular.\n\nTo talk about someone else, change **me** to **te**, **le**, **nos**, **os** or **les**. **A mí**, **a ti**… add emphasis or contrast.\n\nYou can grade the skill: **muy bien**, **bastante bien**, **regular**, **mal**, **fatal**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Se + pronoun + da or dan",
     "texto": [
      "The structure is **se** + pronoun + **da / dan** + **bien / mal**:\n\n- **se me** da / dan: I\n- **se te** da / dan: you\n- **se le** da / dan: he, she, usted\n- **se nos** da / dan: we\n- **se os** da / dan: you (vosotros)\n- **se les** da / dan: they, ustedes\n\nUse **da** with one thing or with an infinitive, and **dan** with several things. To negate, put **no** before **se**: **No se me da bien** el dibujo."
     ],
